 "assembly": "as world.json, then ../weather.dat and ../world_clocks.dat to data/minecraft/, and ../player.dat to players/data/be0f5711-95ac-467f-bac2-a2e5b1c4157c.dat; run every step in order",
 "note": "each step is the settings call to perform and the value read back through the paired accessor; a step marked refused must raise, not comply. The border ops build tags of the listed types in the listed order -- insertion order reaches the digests. A write_world_border_file step names the path it writes: the border is per dimension, under dimensions/<ns>/<dim>/data/minecraft/, never in the world-wide data/minecraft/. Digests are of the UNCOMPRESSED root NBT of each touched file after the whole script, keyed by payload_files, so they are portable.",
